  "question": {
    "text": "The displacement of a particle of mass <math> <mrow> <mtext>3&nbsp;g</mtext> </mrow> </math> executing simple harmonic motion is given by <math><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in SI units. The <math> <mrow> <mtext>KE</mtext> </mrow> </math> of the particle at a point which is at a distance equal to <math> <mrow> <mtext>1/3</mtext> </mrow> </math> of its amplitude from its mean position is"
